WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.180
Whether you have a professional or individual selling account, you're eligible to enroll in FBA.

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:15.038
You can use FBA to store your products in Amazon's fulfillment centers and let us pick, pack and

00:00:15.038 --> 00:00:16.460
ship your FBA orders.

00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:22.200
We'll also handle returns and provide customer service on your behalf for these orders.

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:28.425
With FBA, your items become eligible for Prime Shipping, meaning Amazon Prime customers can benefit

00:00:28.425 --> 00:00:30.740
from free two-day service.

00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:34.940
And all Amazon customers can get free shipping on eligible orders.

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:37.600
This is a great way to maximize

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:39.760
exposure and sales in the Amazon store.

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:42.040
Here's how FBA works.

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:44.707
First, you'll register for FBA and decide

00:00:44.707 --> 00:00:47.860
which products you'd like to send to a fulfillment center.

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:50.815
Note that many but not all products are

00:00:50.815 --> 00:00:56.160
eligible for FBA, even if you're approved to fulfill orders for these products yourself.

00:00:56.780 --> 00:00:57.390
Once you've

00:00:57.390 --> 00:01:02.550
determined which products you'd like to send to Amazon and checked that they're eligible, you'll

00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:04.700
create your first FBA shipment.

00:01:05.260 --> 00:01:09.171
This includes prepping, labeling and packing your products, printing

00:01:09.171 --> 00:01:14.920
box labels, and if you're sending pallet shipments confirming carrier and pallet information.

00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:16.463
Note

00:01:16.463 --> 00:01:21.960
that proper preparation, packaging and labeling can help ensure your products get transported

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:24.600
safely and securely to the fulfillment center.

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:27.440
This will help Amazon make your items available

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:28.860
to customers more quickly.

00:01:29.580 --> 00:01:33.771
When you're ready, send your shipment off to one or more of Amazon's

00:01:33.771 --> 00:01:35.060
fulfillment centers as needed.

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:39.160
After a fulfillment center receives your products, customers can

00:01:39.160 --> 00:01:42.680
begin purchasing your FBA offers in the Amazon store.

00:01:43.340 --> 00:01:45.853
You'll pay fulfillment fees for each unit

00:01:45.853 --> 00:01:50.160
that's picked, packed and shipped to customers from an Amazon fulfillment center.

00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:51.562
These costs

00:01:51.562 --> 00:01:55.980
vary depending on each item's size, weight and category.

00:01:56.920 --> 00:01:59.030
You may also encounter additional fees

00:01:59.030 --> 00:02:01.140
for storing and managing your inventory.

00:02:02.140 --> 00:02:05.961
We'll pack and ship all FBA orders on your behalf and

00:02:05.961 --> 00:02:08.740
handle both customer service and returns for them.

00:02:09.220 --> 00:02:12.365
To put it simply, you sell and Amazon handles the

00:02:12.365 --> 00:02:12.680
rest.

00:02:12.680 --> 00:02:17.999
If a customer returns an item, they'll send it back to the fulfillment center that shipped

00:02:17.999 --> 00:02:22.320
their order and it will be subject to the FBA customer returns policy.

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:24.074
The fulfillment center

00:02:24.074 --> 00:02:29.180
will evaluate the items and return those still in sellable condition to your inventory.

00:02:29.560 --> 00:02:30.000
Some

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:33.960
product categories may incur an FBA returns processing fee.

00:02:34.760 --> 00:02:36.706
We recommend using the revenue

00:02:36.706 --> 00:02:39.820
calculator to estimate these and other FBA costs.

00:02:40.580 --> 00:02:42.180
Ready to learn more about FBA?

00:02:42.780 --> 00:02:43.573
Registered sellers

00:02:43.573 --> 00:02:47.540
can review the FBA product eligibility guide in Seller Central.
